---
title: Tailor CV now shows your fit before it spends a credit
date: 2026-08-15
summary: Clicking Tailor CV first shows your skill match and any location/work-authorization gaps for that job — a free check, no AI involved, before you commit.
type: changelog
tags:
  - cv
  - tailor
  - job-seekers
draft: false
---

Clicking **Tailor CV** used to jump straight into the tailoring workspace. It now shows a
quick check first: which of the job's required skills your profile already covers, which
are missing, and whether anything about the role — location, work mode, work authorization —
doesn't line up with your profile.

None of it calls a model. It's the same deterministic match the job page already computes,
just shown one more time as an explicit "are you sure" before you spend a credit on a role
your own profile might already flag. If everything lines up, the check says so and gets out
of the way. If it doesn't, you can still tailor anyway — nothing is blocked, you just see it
first.

This shows up everywhere **Tailor CV** does: the job page, your applications list, and the
[browser extension](/extension)'s side panel.
